+{
+  "file": "src/agents.ts",
+  "snippet": "toolChoice: 'required',",
+  "cause": "The refundAgent sets toolChoice to 'required', which forces Gemini to emit a function call on every turn, so after approveRefund returns a decline the agent cannot write the customer reply and keeps calling tools until it hits maxTurns.",
+  "evidence": "Running refundAgent against the live model with the refund request and a decline (approved: false, note: 'duplicate claim') reproduced the bug: with 'required' the turn ended in AgentError 'ABORTED: Exceeded maximum tool call iterations (6)' with the model still returning a function call; with 'auto' the same scenario finished with finishReason 'stop' and the reply 'I'm sorry, your refund for order A-1001 was not approved because it appears to be a duplicate claim.'"
+}
